WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.680
Soon the Arrowverse will be missing its namesake
show, as The CW's Arrow will end after eight

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.880
seasons with a final ten-episode run.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.400
The other Arrowverse shows will continue,
at least for now.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.020
But here's why the flagship show is really
ending.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.600
Ratings seem to have played a role in Arrow's
cancellation, but they probably weren't the

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.460
definitive factor.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.119
Viewership numbers have dropped for a few
years, and in 2017 the show was shifted to

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.740
Thursday in the hopes it would get some castoffs
from Supernatural's superior ratings.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.900
Unfortunately, it instead suffered a 14 percent
ratings decline.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:38.239
Viewership dropped off again in 2018, at which
point the question on most fans' minds may

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.160
have been why it wasn't already canceled.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.300
A couple days after the announcement that
Arrow would end, ScreenRant reported that

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.780
while the show continued to lose viewers in
2019, things weren't completely bleak.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.199
In fact, the site reported that statistics
they received from an analytics firm showed

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:58.379
Arrow as the second most successful of CW's
four Arrowverse series at the time of its

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.340
cancellation, coming behind only The Flash.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.140
So while flagging ratings may have contributed
to the end, one would assume that Supergirl

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:08.860
and Legends of Tomorrow would also be cut
if that were the only factor.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:14.240
The term "superhero fatigue" has been thrown
around for a few years now, with people understandably

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.420
wondering exactly when the public is going
to grow tired of caped crusaders.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.580
Arrow may be the victim of a CW-specific version
of this phenomenon.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:29.060
Along with all the Arrowverse shows, the network
also airs Black Lightning, it will soon air

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.440
Batwoman, and there continue to be rumblings
about Superman getting his own CW entry.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.340
The Arrowverse was already crowded, and it's
getting more crowded every year.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.580
One of the factors of the decision to end
Arrow may be that there simply isn't enough

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:42.240
room for it.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:46.860
The timing of the cancellation makes this
possibility more likely considering Batwoman's

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:47.720
pending arrival.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.460
Of all the Arrowverse series, Arrow is usually
the grittiest.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.720
And Batwoman may need to inherit that title
in order to thrive.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.300
Another possible reason for Arrow's finale
is that it's a perfect time to end it.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.790
The Arrowverse is known for its annual crossover
events.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:08.640
The 2018 edition, entitled "Elseworlds," featured
a seemingly godlike being called The Monitor

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.110
who said he was preparing Earth-1 for something
cataclysmic.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.620
"This world will be doomed, like all the others."

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.460
Then the crossover ended with a tease for
the following year's event, which will be

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:24.940
called "Crisis On Infinite Earths."

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:30.560
That's also the name of a classic 1985 comics
story that might be the most important DC

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.080
Comics crossover of all time.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.490
It changed the publisher's entire fictional
landscape, bringing together disparate narratives

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.200
and completely wiping out others.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:44.360
The event was also noteworthy for some prominent
character deaths, which is where Arrow may

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:44.900
come in.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.420
Since the final season will only be 10 episodes,
the finale will probably air close to the

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:50.920
crossover.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.320
Considering the timing, it seems like a good
bet that whatever narrative choices are made

00:02:55.330 --> 00:03:00.370
to wrap up the story of Oliver Queen, possibly
including a heroic death, they'll have a whole

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.360
lot to do with the events of "Crisis."

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.740
Perhaps we shouldn't be asking why Arrow is
ending, but instead why it's even lasted this

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.240
long.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.700
Oliver Queen has walked over the same ground
again and again, literally and figuratively.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.240
There have been hours and hours of flashbacks
to the Island of Lian Yu [lee-ANN YOO] where

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.600
he was "stranded."

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.520
Meanwhile in the present, he and his Team
Arrow buddies have gone back to the island

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.200
so often that it's a little confusing why
they don't just build a summer home there.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:31.560
There have also been countless times when
characters have died and then somehow come

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:35.740
back, or sworn off the crime-fighting game
only to quickly return to it.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.340
But worse than the repetitive plot points
is the ongoing, unconvincing struggle with

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.700
Oliver's darker self.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.240
His inner struggle seems to say that he is
both Hannibal Lecter and the only person who

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.880
can solve the world's problems.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.840
It's a dead horse that the Arrow creative
team finally needs to stop beating.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:52.340
Moving on

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:57.660
According to the show's star Stephen Amell,
the biggest determining factor for ending

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.720
Arrow was Green Arrow himself.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:04.750
Shortly after the announcement that the show's
eighth season would be its last, Amell posted

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.280
a Facebook video to let fans know what had
happened.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:12.260
He revealed that he'd approached producer
Greg Berlanti at the end of the sixth season,

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.060
expressing his wish for season seven to be
the last.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:22.080
"I've always been a fan of television shows
that not only don't overstay their welcome,

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.260
but end in a manner that really packs a punch."

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.780
Fittingly, considering his character has grown
to be much more of a family man over the years,

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:33.470
Amell told viewers that the changes in his
own life behind the camera greatly informed

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.520
his desire for Arrow to conclude.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:40.900
Like the character he plays, he's become a
husband and a father himself, and it's understandably

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.020
been a significant change in his life.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.720
Flashbacks have been one of Arrow's hallmarks
since its first season.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:52.100
But the show switched things up starting in
Season 7, as the premiere ended with a flash-forward

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:57.200
set 20 years in the future with Oliver's grown
son William meeting an older Roy Harper.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.600
Over the course of the season, a story has
been unfolding in the flash-forwards about

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.240
a time when "vigilante" has become a dirty
word.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:07.460
By going forward, Arrow has painted itself
into a corner.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.680
Unless there is some sort of time-traveling
salvation, everyone watching the show knows

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:15.740
how the future looks for its characters, and
it's not good.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:20.940
As one review for CinemaBlend put it, the
flash-forwards potentially took away any reason

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:21.820
to keep watching.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.640
From that perspective, it's best for Arrow
to wrap up quickly before things get any worse.

